// The size of the sheet of paper in lu (1/64 px at 96 dpi) along axis lgax, 0 the width and 1 the height: the page size in twips, converted once.
// By hand: A4 is 11906 twips wide, 11906 * 64 / 15 = 50798 lu, and 16838 high, 71842 lu; a 1500 by 3000 sheet is 6400 by 12800.
lay_sheet(Doc lgd, int lgax) {
  int lgw = lp_lu(lgd.body.page.size[lgax]);
} return int lgw;
given lp_t_new ((import lp_t_d), 0):(50798)
given lp_t_new ((import lp_t_d), 1):(71842)
given lp_t_new given lg_t_page(1500, 3000, 150, 300, 450, 600) ((import lp_t_d), 1):(12800)
